Now paste.test.ts add illegal helper and test. Append before the final test or after. Use `it('finds an illegal move at paste time ...')`.

Helper at top:
```ts
function illegalGame(): string {
  const shuffles = Array.from({ length: 11 }, () => 'Nf3 Nf6 Ng1 Ng8').join(' ');
  return `[Event "Live Chess"]\n[White "Ada"]\n[Black "Nim"]\n[Result "1-0"]\n\n1. ${shuffles} 23. e5 1-0\n`;
}
```
Wait: 44 SANs then "23. e5". Move number before e5 should be 23 (white's 23rd move). That's consistent. Parser ignores numbers. Good.

Add test:
```ts
it('finds an illegal move at paste time and names the game and move', async () => {
  const result = validatePasteBatch([await fixture('checkmate.pgn'), illegalGame()]);
  assert.equal(result.state, 'invalid');
  assert.equal(result.canBuild, false);
  assert.equal(result.slots[0]?.status, 'valid');
  assert.equal(result.slots[1]?.status, 'invalid');
  if (result.slots[1]?.status === 'invalid') {
    assert.equal(result.slots[1].message, 'Game 2, move 23 (e5) is not legal from this position. Check that the PGN came from chess.com.');
  }
  assert.equal(result.summary.total, 1);
  assert.equal(result.summary.includedInStats, 1);
});
```
Would `result.summary` be 1 because valid games exclude illegal. Yes with implementation.

But note the batch message "Fix Game 2 before continuing." Also maybe test legal game passes (already covered).

Use exact string. Fine.

Now report.test.ts. Add helper `illegalPgnAt` after pgnAt. Then test.

Helper:
```ts
function illegalPgnAt(endEpochMs: number): string {
  const shuffles = Array.from({ length: 11 }, () => 'Nf3 Nf6 Ng1 Ng8').join(' ');
  return pgnAt(endEpochMs).replace('1. e4 {[%clk 0:00:50]} 1-0', `1. ${shuffles} 23. e5 1-0`);
}
```
Concern: `String.replace` treats `$` specially; no `$`. Fine.

Test:
```ts
it('refuses a batch with an illegal move before the engine runs', async () => {
  const root = useRoot();
  const samples = Array.from({ length: 46 }, ...);
  const id = await session(root, samples, 45_000_000, EPOCH - 30_000);
  let calls = 0;
  const result = await buildReport(root, id, [pgnAt(EPOCH + 10_000), illegalPgnAt(EPOCH + 20_000)], {
    async evaluate(fen) { calls += 1; return {...}; },
    async close() {},
  });
  assert.equal(result.ok, false);
  if (result.ok) return;
  assert.equal(result.reason, 'illegal_move');
  assert.match(result.remedy, /Game 2, move 23 \(e5\)/);
  assert.equal(calls, 0);
});
```
This test will fail to compile because Refusal reason doesn't include illegal_move and buildReport doesn't return it. Good RED.

Note: the session startEpoch doesn't matter for this test as long as EndTime aligns within 0..45. pgnAt(EPOCH+10_000) creates EndTime based on EPOCH; session start EPOCH; samples 0..45s. legal game end at 10s. illegal game end at 20s. Good. But the illegal game has no clocks; buildReport refuses before align, so fine. pgnAt's date formatting based on epoch. Good.

