Now replace truncation branch in scoreAlignedMoves. Current code lines around 250:

```ts
const position = positions[moveIndex];
if (!position || position.illegal || !position.fenAfter) {
  for (let rest = moveIndex; ...) { ... }
  break;
}
```

Replace with:
```ts
const position = positions[moveIndex];
if (!position || position.illegal || !position.fenAfter) {
  const illegal = firstIllegalMove(sans);
  throw new Error(
    illegal
      ? illegalMoveMessage(aligned.game.index + 1, illegal)
      : `Game ${aligned.game.index + 1} could not be replayed.`,
  );
}
```
But this calls firstIllegalMove which replays; ok in unreachable defensive path. Simpler:
```ts
const illegal = firstIllegalMove(sans);
throw new Error(illegal ? illegalMoveMessage(...) : `Game ... could not be replayed.`);
```
This removes all the truncation code. Then `moveTimes.find` still used below for the legal path. Good.

