options.spawnWorker?: () => Worker
```
Default spawns engine-worker. Then engine uses `spawnWorker` for both initial and restarts. Keep `worker` option? Existing tests pass `worker` to simulate hang. We can keep it as the first worker; on restart use spawnWorker. For a hang test, no crash, so no restart needed. For crash test, pass `spawnWorker` only. Remove `worker`? Existing test uses `worker` and then terminates in finally. Keep for compatibility.

Crash flow:
```ts
const onError = () => {
  if (settled) return;
  cleanupListener;
  if (worker === current) worker = undefined;
  if (restartsUsed < maxRestarts) {
    restartsUsed += 1;
    // retry same fen with a fresh worker
    finishAttempt? 
