```

Signature:
```ts
export async function buildReport(root, sessionId, pgns, engine?, control: ReportBuildControl = {}): Promise<Report | Refusal>
```
At start after snapshot: if signal aborted return cancelledRefusal.
Before save: check signal.

Pass signal to engine if creating: `createEngine({ signal: control.signal })`. If an injected engine is provided, tests handle it.

`const scoredMoves = await scoreAlignedMoves(..., scorer, control);`
If cancelled → refusal.

Add `engine: scoredMoves.engine` to report parse.

`scoreAlignedMoves` signature adds control. Return `ScoreOutcome`.

Refactor the body. Let me write the new `scoreAlignedMoves` entirely.

```ts
async function scoreAlignedMoves(
  games: readonly { game: { index; moves: {san; clockSec?}[]; timeControl?; includeInStats } }[],
  moveTimes: readonly { gameIndex; moveIndex; tUs }[],
  samples: readonly PulseSample[],
  baseline: number,
  engine: Evaluator,
  control: ReportBuildControl,
): Promise<ScoreOutcome> {
  const planned = games
    .filter((entry) => entry.game.includeInStats)
    .map((entry) => {
      const sans = entry.game.moves.map((move) => move.san);
      return {
        aligned: entry,
        sans,
        thinks: thinkTimeSec(entry.game),
        positions: positionsFromMoves(sans),
      };
    });

  const total = countPositions(planned);
  const cache = new Map<string, Promise<PositionEval>>();
  const counted = new Set<string>();
  const reasons = { timeout: 0, crash: 0, engine: 0, budget: 0 };
  let scoredPositions = 0;

  const evaluate = (fen: string): Promise<PositionEval> => {
    const cached = cache.get(fen);
    if (cached) return cached;
    const pending = engine.evaluate(fen).then((result) => {
      if (!counted.has(fen)) {
        counted.add(fen);
        if (result.evalFailed) {
          if (result.reason === 'timeout') reasons.timeout += 1;
          else if (result.reason === 'crash') reasons.crash += 1;
          else if (result.reason === 'budget') reasons.budget += 1;
          else reasons.engine += 1;
        } else {
          scoredPositions += 1;
        }
        control.onProgress?.({ scored: scoredPositions, total });
      }
      return result;
    });
    cache.set(fen, pending);
    return pending;
  };

  control.onProgress?.({ scored: 0, total });

  const metrics: MoveMetric[] = [];
  const elevatedBlunderTimes: (number | null)[] = [];
  const timelineMoves: TimelineMove[] = [];

  for (const { aligned, sans, thinks, positions } of planned) {
    for (let moveIndex = 0; moveIndex < sans.length; moveIndex += 1) {
      const position = positions[moveIndex];
      if (!position || position.illegal || !position.fenAfter) {
        const illegal = firstIllegalMove(sans);
        throw new Error(...);
      }
      const when = moveTimes.find(...);
      const before = await evaluate(position.fenBefore);
      if (before.reason === 'cancelled' || control.signal?.aborted) return { cancelled: true };
      const after: Score = position.terminalAfter
        ? { evalFailed:false, terminal: position.terminalAfter }
        : await evaluate(position.fenAfter);
      if (after.reason === 'cancelled' || control.signal?.aborted) return { cancelled: true };
      ...
    }
  }
  const failed = reasons.timeout + reasons.crash + reasons.engine + reasons.budget;
  return {
    cancelled: false,
    metrics,
    elevatedBlunderTimes,
    timelineMoves,
    engine: { positions: total, scored: scoredPositions, failed, reasons },
  };
}
```

Wait: `Score` doesn't have `reason`. `after` typed Score. Checking `after.reason` fails. Use PositionEval type for after:
```ts
const before = await evaluate(...);
...
let after: Score;
if (position.terminalAfter) after = {...};
else {
  const evaluated = await evaluate(position.fenAfter);
  if (evaluated.reason === 'cancelled' || control.signal?.aborted) return { cancelled:true };
  after = evaluated;
}
```
And `before.reason` is PositionEval. Good.

Also check signal before evaluating before:
```ts
if (control.signal?.aborted) return { cancelled: true };
```

`countPositions(planned)`:
```ts
function countPositions(planned: readonly { positions: readonly MovePosition[] }[]): number {
  const fens = new Set<string>();
  for (const entry of planned) {
    for (const position of entry.positions) {
      if (!position || position.illegal || !position.fenAfter) continue;
      fens.add(position.fenBefore);
      if (!position.terminalAfter) fens.add(position.fenAfter);
    }
  }
  return fens.size;
}
```
Need import `MovePosition` type from positions, or inline structural type. Use:
```ts
import { firstIllegalMove, illegalMoveMessage, positionsFromMoves, type MovePosition } from './analysis/positions.js';
```

Cancellation refusal helper:
```ts
const CANCELLED: Refusal = { ok:false, reason:'cancelled', remedy:'Report build cancelled. The previous report was kept.' };
```
But if there was no previous report, "kept" is still technically true (nothing replaced). Fine. Maybe "Nothing was saved." Better: "Report build cancelled. No report was saved." But if previous exists, it remains. Say "Report build cancelled. The previous report, if any, was kept." Slightly wordy. Keep "Report build cancelled. No report was saved."

Return at:
- top if signal aborted.
- after scoring cancelled.
- before save if aborted.

Also, progress events during scoring may fire after cancel? Cache promises already in flight could resolve after cancellation and call onProgress. The engine aborts current; others in queue? Because evaluate is sequential queue, after cancel each returns cancelled. The `.then` in evaluate could call onProgress with reason cancelled → counted as `engine` reason. But build returns cancelled; stats discarded. Progress could emit increasing counts after cancel. The UI will stop showing after build ends. Fine.

Potential double-count: `counted` set ensures each unique FEN counted once. But if a FEN was cached before the `counted` check? We only set cache on first call, and the `.then` runs once per cache entry. Good.

`total` includes unique FENs, but if some before FEN equals an after FEN, dedupe. Good.

Now engine stats `positions: total`, `scored: scoredPositions`. If some FENs are never evaluated because cancellation, report not produced. Fine.

One nuance: `evaluate` cache key is the FEN string, but a position may be evaluated as `before` and later as `after`; the engine score perspective differs by side to move, which is encoded in the FEN. Same FEN = same side to move and position; safe.

