```ts
function linearBandAt(samples, tUs, baseline) {
  let latest: PulseSample | undefined;
  for (const entry of samples) {
    if (entry.tUs <= tUs && (!latest || entry.tUs >= latest.tUs)) latest = entry;
  }
  if (!latest || !(latest.stable && latest.confidence >= 80)) return null;
  if (tUs > latest.tUs + SAMPLE_HOLD_US) return null;
  return latest.bpm >= baseline + 10 ? 'elevated' : 'settled';
}
```
Wait, `bandFor` threshold: ELEVATED_MARGIN_BPM from bands.ts. Import it, or use `bandFor`. The oracle should use the old code exactly, including `isUsableSample(latest, CONFIDENCE_FLOOR)` and `bandFor`. Import `bandFor` and `CONFIDENCE_FLOOR`? report.test already imports SAMPLE_HOLD_US from sensing. `isUsableSample` is in session.ts (used by report). For the oracle, use the same semantics:
```ts
import { bandFor } from './analysis/bands.js';
import { CONFIDENCE_FLOOR, SAMPLE_HOLD_US } from '../shared/sensing.js';
```
Currently only SAMPLE_HOLD_US. Add CONFIDENCE_FLOOR. Oracle:
