Duplicates at 4_000_000: weak first (confidence 10) then usable 90. Stable sort keeps weak then usable; binary upper bound picks usable (last equal). Linear oracle: iterates, for first weak at 4m picks; then usable at 4m with `>=` picks usable (last). Both 'elevated' (90). Good. If reversed, both would pick weak? Stable sort preserves original order; last equal is usable. Fine.

