```ts
function clockText(seconds: number): string {
  const hours = Math.floor(seconds / 3600);
  const minutes = Math.floor((seconds % 3600) / 60);
  const rest = seconds % 60;
  return `${hours}:${String(minutes).padStart(2, '0')}:${String(rest).padStart(2, '0')}`;
}

function longPgnAt(endEpochMs: number): string {
  const end = new Date(endEpochMs);
  const pad = (value: number) => String(value).padStart(2, '0');
  const date = `${end.getUTCFullYear()}.${pad(end.getUTCMonth() + 1)}.${pad(end.getUTCDate())}`;
  const time = `${pad(end.getUTCHours())}:${pad(end.getUTCMinutes())}:${pad(end.getUTCSeconds())}`;
  const moves: string[] = [];
  for (let full = 0; full < 80; full += 1) {
    const san = full % 2 === 0 ? ['Nf3', 'Nf6'] : ['Ng1', 'Ng8'];
    const sec = 5399 - full;
    moves.push(`${full + 1}. ${san[0]} {[%clk ${clockText(sec)}]} ${san[1]} {[%clk ${clockText(sec)}]}`);
  }
  return `[Event "Live Chess"]
[White "Ada"]
[Black "Nim"]
[Result "1-0"]
[TimeControl "5400"]
[Termination "Ada won by resignation"]
[EndDate "${date}"]
[EndTime "${time}"]

${moves.join(' ')} 1-0
`;
}
```
Wait: SAN sequence `Nf3 Nf6` then `Ng1 Ng8` then `Nf3`... Legal? After move 1 Nf3, black Nf6; move 2 white Ng1 (knight f3 to g1), black Ng8 (knight f6 to g8); move 3 white Nf3 again, etc. Yes.

`thinkTimeSec`: white clocks for full moves 0..79: 5399, 5398, ..., 5320. First white think = 5400 - 5399 = 1; next white previous 5399 - 5398 = 1; ... total 80. Black same. Duration 160s = 160_000_000 µs.

But note the clocks for white and black in the same full move are both `sec`; black's previous clock is its clock from the prior full move (5399 -> 5398), so 1. Good.

Session 90 min: samples 5401 at 1s; stop 5_400_000_000 µs. EndTime EPOCH + 5_400_000 ms.

