content.text:
Providers changes:
1. OpenCode max_tokens.
2. Response schema + reasoning error.

Edit request body:
```ts
...(config.provider === 'custom' ? { max_tokens: 500 } : { max_completion_tokens: 500 }),
```
→
```ts
// OpenAI recommends max_completion_tokens; OpenCode's OpenAI-compatible examples use max_tokens.
...(config.provider === 'openai' ? { max_completion_tokens: 500 } : { max_tokens: 500 }),
```
This covers opencode and custom.

Response schema and parse. Current:
```ts
const openAiResponse = z.object({
  choices: z.array(z.object({ message: z.object({ content: z.string().min(1) }) })).min(1),
});
...
} else {
  const parsed = openAiResponse.safeParse(value);
  if (parsed.success) text = parsed.data.choices[0].message.content;
}
```
New:
```ts
const openAiMessage = z.object({
  content: z.string().nullable().optional(),
  reasoning: z.unknown().optional(),
  reasoning_content: z.unknown().optional(),
  refusal: z.string().nullable().optional(),
});
const openAiResponse = z.object({
  choices: z.array(z.object({ message: openAiMessage })).min(1),
});
```
Parse:
```ts
} else {
  const parsed = openAiResponse.safeParse(value);
  if (parsed.success) {
    const message = parsed.data.choices[0]?.message;
    if (message?.content && message.content.trim().length > 0) {
      text = message.content;
    } else if (message && (message.reasoning !== undefined || message.reasoning_content !== undefined)) {
      throw new AiProviderError(
        'The AI provider returned reasoning but no final answer. Try a different model.',
        false,
      );
    } else if (message?.refusal && message.refusal.trim().length > 0) {
      throw new AiProviderError(
        'The AI provider refused the request. Nothing in this report depends on it.',
        false,
      );
    }
  }
}
```
Note: z.object by default strips unknown keys; `message.reasoning` will be present if defined. Good.
What if `content` is an array (newer APIs)? The schema rejects; then unreadable. Chat Completions content can be string or array of parts. The adapter only expects string; fine.
What if content null, no reasoning, no refusal? falls through to unreadable. Good.
What if content null and reasoning empty string? `reasoning !== undefined` true; explicit reasoning error. Good.

Also system prompt: add a line "Do not mention medical or diagnostic terms, and do not claim to know the player's mental or physical state." It already says "Do not diagnose health or claim to know a mental state." Fine. Could strengthen with "Never use words like anxiety, stress, heart rate, or diagnosis." The validator handles it. Add? The system prompt is already sufficient. Keep.

Edit.

