Finding 5 valid: move `mate` before guard. Finding 6: current `analyseMoves` uses `accuracy === null` and `bandSummary` filters accuracy. Need to verify `bandSummary`:
```ts
const scored = moves.filter(move => move.band === band && move.accuracy !== null);
```
Yes, already includes mate moves. The finding says "Update the aggregation predicates ... to include moves with available accuracy even when CPL is null... handle CPL aggregation separately without requiring it for inclusion." Current code doesn't reference CPL in aggregation. So skip finding 6 as already satisfied. But maybe `MoveMetric.mate` moves have `accuracy` non-null only if both evals available; yes. We can add a test assertion that a mate move contributes to `scored`/`blunders` even with cpl null. Existing metrics.test has a mate unscored case but not a scored mate. Add a test to prove and document. Maybe no code change needed. We can note skip, but adding a regression is good.

Fix 5:
```ts
const mate = mateInvolved(before) || mateInvolved(after);
const beforeCp = ...
if (beforeCp === null || afterCp === null) return {..., mate, ...};
```
Add test:
```ts
it('preserves mate involvement when the other evaluation fails', () => {
  const move = scoreMove(failed, {evalFailed:false, mate:1}, 'settled', true);
  assert.equal(move.mate, true);
  assert.equal(move.cpl, null);
  assert.equal(move.accuracy, null);
  assert.equal(move.blunder, false);
});
```
